CORE
main.sh

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[shell-arithmetic\.[0-9]+\] .*value of \$__cprover_arithmetic_0 is an integer constant .*: FAILURE$
^\[assertion\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A command substitution in arithmetic runs first, and its output, which
is not modelled, is checked to be an integer constant (it could
otherwise be any expression, even an assignment).
